WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Hi, I'm Chen Xiazi. Grandma just watered the flowers. The dirt near the roots looks darker, the dirt by the path looks lighter.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:56.000
The little girl crouches by the path. Dry dirt near her shoes is yellowish-brown. Wet dirt by the roots is deep brown. A pale gray stone sits in between.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Grandma scoops dry dirt from the same spot into two white dishes. The little girl spreads it into two even piles side by side.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:56.000
She drips a few drops of water into the right dish. The wet dirt looks darker. Most dirt looks darker when it gets wet.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Now let's mix the first color. Start with a little yellow-ochre, add a tiny bit of brown and white, mix a light yellowish-brown.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Next, the wet-dirt color. Darken part of the light mix with more brown. Compare light and dark on the same paper.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:44.000
The third stroke is for the little stone. Add a tiny bit of black to white for pale gray, then a speck of yellowish-brown.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Turn it into a small patch of ground. Paint a big area of light yellowish-brown, a patch of deep brown, and a few pale gray stones.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:05:00.000
The little girl shows Grandma her painting. The darkest color came from the dirt she just watered. Write the place and a note so you can find it again.
